        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.53,
          "end": 204.293,
          "en": "Julie Jones, also with a random phone number here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.3,
          "end": 208.1,
          "en": "And again, this is all really up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.1,
          "end": 209.933,
          "en": "And here I have julie@localhost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.96,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "So now we got data in our app config object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 219.53,
          "en": "And if we leave aside how we use this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.53,
          "end": 221.9,
          "en": "because currently we're not using it at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.9,
          "end": 223.98,
          "en": "except for storing it in this constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 223.98,
          "end": 227.31,
          "en": "If we leave that aside, it's just what we learned, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 227.31,
          "end": 230,
          "en": "We have an object with a data method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230,
          "end": 231.93,
          "en": "where we return the data object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.93,
          "end": 234.643,
          "en": "So that's all what we learned before as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.31,
          "end": 242.02,
          "en": "Now this should be the config object for our main app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 242.02,
          "end": 246.94,
          "en": "How do we now get this config object in the App.vue file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.94,
          "end": 250.903,
          "en": "into our create app method in main JS?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.78,
          "end": 257.03,
          "en": "Well, we're going to use this import syntax here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.03,
          "end": 258.96,
          "en": "which you already see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 258.96,
          "end": 261.6,
          "en": "This is a modern JavaScript feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.6,
          "end": 265.72,
          "en": "which we use in Vue CLI created Vue projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 265.72,
          "end": 268.81,
          "en": "to combine different JavaScript files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.81,
          "end": 271.81,
          "en": "and export a feature in one file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 271.81,
          "end": 272.913,
          "en": "and use it in another.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.13,
          "end": 279.11,
          "en": "For that, we import something from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.11,
          "end": 282.27,
          "en": "and then you point at the file from what you want to import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.27,
          "end": 285.15,
          "en": "And here you should use a relative import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.15,
          "end": 287.2,
          "en": "starting with ./,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.2,
          "end": 290.68,
          "en": "which means it's in the same folder as this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 290.68,
          "end": 291.72,
          "en": "and then the file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.72,
          "end": 294.053,
          "en": "In this case, App.vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 295.52,
          "end": 297.75,
          "en": "The import here looks a bit different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.75,
          "end": 299.86,
          "en": "It's not ./vue here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 299.86,
          "end": 302.61,
          "en": "because here we're importing from a package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 302.61,
          "end": 304.61,
          "en": "from this Vue package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 304.61,
          "end": 306.54,
          "en": "And if you're importing from a package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 306.54,
          "end": 308.63,
          "en": "you just reference the package name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.63,
          "end": 310.75,
          "en": "But if you're importing from a custom file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 310.75,
          "end": 314.983,
          "en": "like App.vue, you specify the path to that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 316,
          "end": 319.64,
          "en": "Now that ... is not the valid syntax though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 319.64,
          "end": 323.53,
          "en": "Instead, we could import a named export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 323.53,
          "end": 328.53,
          "en": "by using curly braces or a default export.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.56,
          "end": 330.4,
          "en": "Now you might not know what the difference is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 330.4,
          "end": 333.63,
          "en": "Here, we're going to use a default export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.63,
          "end": 336.96,
          "en": "by just coming up with any name of our choice here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 336.96,
          "end": 338.8,
          "en": "and importing that from that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 338.8,
          "end": 341.08,
          "en": "And this identifier here is really up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 341.08,
          "end": 342.36,
          "en": "It could be hello.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 342.36,
          "end": 344.40999999999997,
          "en": "It could be something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 344.40999999999997,
          "end": 348,
          "en": "But typically you name it just like the file was named",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348,
          "end": 351.15999999999997,
          "en": "because in there we have our main app configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.15999999999997,
          "end": 353.89,
          "en": "So I'm going to name it App here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 353.89,
          "end": 356.58,
          "en": "And this is now what we pass to create app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.58,
          "end": 359.27,
          "en": "because App, what we import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.27,
          "end": 363.14,
          "en": "should just be this JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 363.14,
          "end": 366.06,
          "en": "this Vue config JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 366.06,
          "end": 369.1,
          "en": "However, at the moment, we're not exporting this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 369.1,
          "end": 373.99,
          "en": "To export it, we should rather not store it in a constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 373.99,
          "end": 376.7,
          "en": "which would only be available in this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 376.7,
          "end": 380.42,
          "en": "and not in any other file, but instead we use a syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.42,
          "end": 384.07,
          "en": "which is also default modern JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 384.07,
          "end": 389.07,
          "en": "Export, the export keyword and then the default keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 389.52,
          "end": 393.06,
          "en": "And this tells JavaScript that this object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 393.06,
          "end": 397.233,
          "en": "is the default export of this App.vue file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 398.49,
          "end": 401.14,
          "en": "And that means that whenever we import like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 401.14,
          "end": 403.28,
          "en": "we're going to import that default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 403.28,
          "end": 406.26,
          "en": "So we're going to import that object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 406.26,
          "end": 409.86,
          "en": "So we're sharing this object from the App.vue file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 409.86,
          "end": 411.64,
          "en": "to the main JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 411.64,
          "end": 412.86,
          "en": "And therefore, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 412.86,
          "end": 417.86,
          "en": "we passed this config object to create App here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
